// ONE COPY OF THE LOADER, REACHED TWO WAYS. The template combo box in
// the dialog header selects a template and calls this; a host seeding a
// brand new request from a category calls the LoadTemplate action, which
// sets the same variable and selects the same button. The body lives here
// so the two entry points cannot drift apart.
//
// KEYED ON _cmpWfSeedKey, NOT ON THE COMBO BOX SELECTION, because the
// action route has no selection to read. The combo box writes the
// variable before selecting this.
//
// BLANK OR UNKNOWN KEY IS A NO OP, so an existing request can call
// LoadTemplate unconditionally right after LoadDraft without knowing
// whether it has a template.
//
// Completed phases SURVIVE a template load. Replacing a finished
// phase would discard work Flow has already recorded. The template
// appends after whatever is locked.
//
// Every ParseJSON read is explicitly cast. A missing field returns
// Blank() with no error, so an uncast read fails silently. JSON
// field names are case sensitive.
//
// CLIENTID IS KEYED ON POSITION, NOT ON a.order. PARALLEL WORKERS SHARE
// AN ORDER: two assignments in one phase at the same order is how this app
// expresses "these run together", and the shipped data does exactly that,
// Finance Reviewer and Technical Reviewer both at order 1.
//
// 200000 + phase * 1000 + Value(a.order) therefore produced an IDENTICAL
// ClientId for both rows. ClientId is what the edit dialog looks a row up
// by, so editing one parallel worker PATCHED THE OTHER, and where the
// other already held that value nothing changed at all and the edit
// vanished with no error. UnresolvedCount could then never reach zero, so
// Save stayed disabled permanently.
//
// THIS IS THE SAME DEFECT LoadDraft ALREADY FIXED for loaded rows, left
// behind on the template path. It only became reachable once the loader
// gained a second entry point and started running for every new request.
//
// Sequence over the assignment COUNT gives a per-phase position that is
// unique by construction; Index reads the untyped element positionally.
//
// Assignees arrive UNRESOLVED: role holds a role or group name and
// the payload has no email. The footer counts them and Save stays
// disabled until each is picked.
//
// THIS IS DESTRUCTIVE for unlocked work and there is no confirm
// step. See the notes shipped with this file if you want one.

